/*  The snake game — the vertical slice: a model in its own file, and a main that draws it.

    ⚠ Not a game yet. It draws one frame of a body that never moves, which is the smallest thing
    that proves the structure: a type crossing a file boundary, and a blueprint that builds them
    together.

    ⚠⚠ THE VIEW IS NOT ITS OWN FILE YET, and that is a language limitation rather than a choice.
    A module written inside a pull cannot name the pulled module's carried type in its own
    SIGNATURE — `Bind series of text to frame-of, given (the series of spot body)` is refused with
    "'spot' is not a defined type", though the same type resolves fine inside a method BODY.
    MEASURED 2026-09-20. Until that is fixed the drawing lives here, where `spot` is in scope.
*/

Pull board.
    Define body as a series of spot.
    Insert cast board's at on (4, 8) into body.
    Insert cast board's at on (4, 9) into body.
    Insert cast board's at on (4, 10) into body.

    State "a {cast board's height} by {cast board's width} field:".

    For each row in range 1 to cast board's height, repeat:
        Define line as "".
        For each column in range 1 to cast board's width, repeat:
            Define here as cast board's at on (row, column).
            Define filled as false.
            For each piece in body, repeat:
                If cast piece's same-as on (here), the filled becomes true.
            Done.
            If filled, the line becomes line joined to "O".
            Otherwise, the line becomes line joined to ".".
        Done.
        State line.
    Done.
Done.
